load @term/seed/code/structure/ring
  find ring

# A Hecke algebra: a deformation of the group algebra of a Coxeter group, where the generators satisfy a quadratic
# relation interpolating between a reflection and the identity by a parameter. Hecke algebras govern the representation
# theory of groups of Lie type and underlie the Jones polynomial of knots. Since the Weyl group of F4 is the symmetry of
# the 24-cell, its Hecke algebra is tied to the substrate's symmetry. The form carries the underlying ring.
form hecke-algebra
  link ring, like ring
